{{!
    @template local_moodesk/breadcrumb

    The Breadcrumb — where a deep screen sits in the product.

    The shell renders on Moodle's `embedded` layout, which draws no navbar, so
    until the knowledge base's article page nothing in mooDesk was more than
    one step from its sidebar entry and nothing needed one. It follows the
    WAI-ARIA Authoring Practices pattern: a <nav> with an accessible name, an
    ordered list, links for every step but the last, which is the current
    page and plain text with aria-current. Separators are drawn by CSS so
    they are not read aloud.

    Context variables:
      * label   - Accessible name of the navigation ("Breadcrumb")
      * items[] - {label, url, current}. `current` is true on the last item only,
                  which then renders as text rather than a link.

    Example context (json):
    {
      "label": "Breadcrumb",
      "items": [
        {"label": "Knowledge base", "url": "/local/moodesk/kb.php", "current": false},
        {"label": "Access", "url": "/local/moodesk/kb.php?category=3", "current": false},
        {"label": "How to reset your password", "url": null, "current": true}
      ]
    }
}}
<nav class="mhd-breadcrumb" aria-label="{{label}}">
  <ol class="mhd-breadcrumb__list">
    {{#items}}
    <li class="mhd-breadcrumb__item">
      {{#current}}<span class="mhd-breadcrumb__current" aria-current="page">{{label}}</span>{{/current}}
      {{^current}}<a class="mhd-breadcrumb__link" href="{{url}}">{{label}}</a>{{/current}}
    </li>
    {{/items}}
  </ol>
</nav>
